14, 2026.</em></p><p><strong>Georgia law sets out when a person occupying land can claim title by adverse possession, and how an owner can remove someone who has no right to be there.</strong></p><h2>What the official sources say</h2><ul><li>Unlawful squatting (O.C.G.A. 16-7-21.1, enacted by HB 1017, effective Apr 24, 2024): entering and residing on another&#x27;s land or premises without the owner&#x27;s or rightful occupant&#x27;s knowledge or consent is a misdemeanor. (HB 1017 (Georgia Squatter Reform Act), 16-7-21.1(a)-(b); <a href='https://gov.georgia.gov/document/2024-signed-legislation/hb-1017/download' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>An accused squatter gets a citation and must show properly executed documentation (lease or proof of rent payments) to the issuing agency within 3 business days or is subject to arrest; if documentation is submitted, a hearing is set within 7 days. (HB 1017, 16-7-21.1(a)(2)-(4); <a href='https://gov.georgia.gov/document/2024-signed-legislation/hb-1017/download' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Owner removal of an intruder: affidavit of good-faith right of possession; the sheriff or certified officer turns the person out once 3 days have elapsed from exhibition of the affidavit, unless the occupant files a counteraffidavit, which sends both affidavits to court for trial. (HB 1017, O.C.G.A. 44-11-30 and 44-11-32 as revised; <a href='https://gov.georgia.gov/document/2024-signed-legislation/hb-1017/download' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>If the court finds the occupant&#x27;s counteraffidavit not meritorious by a preponderance, the occupant is removed under a writ of possession and the court may award fair market rent for the occupancy. (HB 1017, O.C.G.A. 44-11-32(a)(2)-(3); <a href='https://gov.georgia.gov/document/2024-signed-legislation/hb-1017/download' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li></ul><div class=\"chb-cta\" style=\"margin:32px 0;border-radius:10px;background:linear-gradient(120deg,#0F1C2E 0%,#16293F 100%);padding:28px 32px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;flex-wrap:wrap;color:#fff;\"><div style=\"max-width:600px;\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:2px;color:#E0A83C;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:6px;\">Selling in Georgia?</div><div style=\"font-weight:800;font-size:20px;line-height:1.35;color:#fff;\">We buy Georgia houses as-is, with no commission, no repairs and no closing costs to you.</div></div><a href=\"#\" onclick=\"var f=document.querySelector('iframe[data-form-id]');if(f){f.scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth',block:'center'});return false;}\" style=\"flex-shrink:0;padding:14px 24px;border-radius:8px;background:#E0A83C;color:#16203A;font-size:14px;font-weight:800;text-decoration:none;white-space:nowrap;\">Get My Cash Offer &rarr;</a></div><h2>Georgia Squatters Rights and Adverse Possession FAQ</h2><h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Can a squatter take ownership of my Georgia house?</h3><p> Check the statute and talk to a Georgia attorney about your facts.</p><div class='wsp-related'><div class='wsp-related-grid'><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/georgia-landlord-tenant-law-tenant-rights/'>Georgia Landlord Tenant Law and Tenant Rights</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/georgia-eviction-notice/'>Georgia Eviction Notice: Types and Days</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/georgia-guides-by-city-and-county/'>Georgia guides by city and county</a><p>Every local guide we publish.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/we-buy-houses-in-georgia/'>We buy houses in Georgia</a><p>How a cash offer works.</p></div></div></div><h2>Sources</h2><ul><li><a href='https://gov.georgia.gov/document/2024-signed-legislation/hb-1017/download' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>HB 1017 (Georgia Squatter Reform Act), 16-7-21.1(a)-(b)</a></li></ul><p><em>General information for Georgia Squatters Rights and Adverse Possession, not legal or tax advice. Confirm details with the official office or a licensed professional.</em></p><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"FAQPage\", \"mainEntity\": [{\"@type\": \"Question\", \"name\": \"Can a squatter take ownership of my Georgia house?\", \"acceptedAnswer\": {\"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"Only by meeting every requirement of the adverse possession statute cited above for the full period. Check the statute and talk to a Georgia attorney about your facts.\"}}]}</script><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"BreadcrumbList\", \"itemListElement\": [{\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 1, \"name\": \"Home\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 2, \"name\": \"Georgia\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/we-buy-houses-in-georgia/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 3, \"name\": \"Georgia Squatters Rights and Adverse Possession\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/georgia-squatters-rights-adverse-possession/\"}]}</script></div>\n<!-- /wp:html -->", "status": "publish", "rank_math_title": "Georgia Squatters Rights and Adverse Possession", "rank_math_description": "Georgia squatters rights and adverse possession: what the statutes say and how owners remove occupants or sell. Official sources.", "rank_math_focus_keyword": "georgia squatters rights"}, {"slug": "georgia-landlord-tenant-law-tenant-rights", "title": "Georgia Landlord Tenant Law and Tenant Rights: Rules for Selling a Rental", "content": "<!-- wp:html -->\n<style>.wsp-hero{position:relative;margin:0 calc(-50vw + 50%);padding:5rem 1.5rem;background-image:none;backgroun